# The case of every code point, in Unicode 17.0.0: the one-to-one mappings to
# upper, lower and title case, and the characters whose case is several
# characters. `casing.hero` reads them.
#
# Generated, never edited by hand: the Heroes program
# `rebel/generators/unicode_tables/` read the Unicode Character Database 17.0.0
# (https://www.unicode.org/Public/17.0.0/ucd/, fetched 2026-11-22), its
# files `UnicodeData.txt` and `SpecialCasing.txt`, reduced them to ranges,
# held every lookup to the files' answer for each of the 1,114,112 code points,
# and wrote this module whole; its `check` command says whether this module is
# still what it writes.
#
# Each entry is one range, `first << 22 | last << 1 | step - 1`: the code
# points from `first` to `last`, every one where `step` is 1 and every second
# where it is 2, in ascending order.

# The ranges of code points that have an upper case of one code point other
# than themselves.
